<article class="env-lemma" id="0A5V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A5V">Lemma <span data-tag="0A5V">15.71.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K \in D(R)$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $K$ is in $D^ b(R)$ and $H^ i(K)$ has finite injective dimension for all $i$, then $K$ has finite injective dimension. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $K^\bullet $ represents $K$, is a bounded complex of $R$-modules, and $K^ i$ has finite injective dimension for all $i$, then $K$ has finite injective dimension. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: Apply the spectral sequences of Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015J" data-tag="015J">13.21.3</a> to the functor $F = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(N, -)$ to get a computation of $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_ A(N, K)$ and use the criterion of Lemma <a href="/tag/0A5T" data-tag="0A5T">15.71.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>